KG42.register("rules-a39c412bb0e9ee2507d2cf5f",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R002","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Demand submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The aggregator performs demand submission by announcing the power required for the next hour to registered agents. Scope: Hour-ahead reverse auction for the microgrid lumped load. Condition: The required load for each upcoming hour is assumed correctly estimated.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.demand under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.demand","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Hour-ahead reverse auction for the microgrid lumped load.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator performs demand submission by announcing the power required for the next hour to registered agents. Scope: Hour-ahead reverse auction for the microgrid lumped load. Condition: The required load for each upcoming hour is assumed correctly estimated.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"GAME THEORY 1067 Algorithm 1 Agent Negotiations Begin Initialize: All available generators register ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Agent Negotiations\nBegin\nInitialize: All available generators register to yellow page;\nLoop\nAggregator agent: inform utility base price, power demand for next hour;\nAggregator agent: request bids;\nif (DER base price \u003c utility base price) then\nBidder agents: inform submit bids;\nelse\nBidder agent: drop not participating;\nend"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"terminated. All available generators in the microgrid should 1) register to the yellow pages in orde","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"A reverse auction model has been implemented and realistically operated. Algorithm 1 briefly expresses the simplified pseudo code of the proposed reverse auction model. In Algorithm 1, the process is continuous unless the program is terminated. All available generators in the microgrid should register to the yellow pages in order to participate in bidding processes. The required amount of load is assumed to be correctly estimated for each upcoming hour; therefore the aggregator agent has this information ready to inform all agents registered to the yellow page. The main purpose of the aggregator agent is to purchase the required amount of energy with the least cost. The aggregator agent collects the submitted bids and checks whether the submitted supply matches the demand."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The rule describes an aggregator announcement action, not a design selection or operational decision variable. The frozen graph declares no x objects, and the source supplies no symbol or domain for the announced demand quantity within this rule scope.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed constant or parameter is defined for demand submission in this rule scope. The demand is described only as an estimated input for each upcoming hour, without a symbol, value, or unit definition tied to the demand-submission rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","quote":"Aggregator agent: inform utility base price, power demand for next hour;"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","quote":"The required amount of load is assumed to be correctly estimated for each upcoming hour; therefore the aggregator agent has this information ready to inform all agents registered to the yellow page."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"d0a1669c4465a1ec397a08cea5d918a9abf3720abb813b1999a2457641b7a376","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The source-supported content of this rule is procedural: the aggregator announces the correctly estimated next-hour power demand to agents registered in the yellow pages. The supplied evidence states the announcing action and the estimated-demand condition, but provides no symbolic demand variable, formula, domain, unit, or parameter definition specific to this rule. Therefore the existing constraint remains not_formalized and the rule is classified as non_mathematical rather than inferring unsupported mathematics.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The procedural constraint records the aggregator's announcement of next-hour required power to registered agents. It binds the acting coordinator to coordination.local_operator and the demand-submission action/object to bidding.demand, with the frozen links edge v141-c-R002-E001 representing that relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
